wifi: mt76: compat: build the NAN code as stubs on pre-7.1 hosts

The Linux 7.3 mt76 sources the DKMS package extracts carry NAN support for the
MT7925, written against cfg80211 interfaces that arrived in Linux 7.1: the NAN
data interface type (NL80211_IFTYPE_NAN_DATA), the NAN peer schedule limits
(CFG80211_NAN_MAX_PEER_MAPS, CFG80211_NAN_SCHED_NUM_TIME_SLOTS), the peer's
NMI station pointer and the nan_peer_sched_changed() callback. Building against
a 6.17 through 7.0 host fails with undeclared identifiers.

Kbuild defines MT76_NO_NAN when the host's nl80211.h lacks
NL80211_IFTYPE_NAN_DATA, which tests the symbol and so also handles a distro
kernel that backported it. In that case the NAN-only code is not compiled, the
NAN entry points in nan.c become stubs, and the wiphy does not advertise NAN,
so none of them is reached. Behaviour on a 7.1 or newer host is unchanged.

